    "name": "flowconx_client_disjoint",
    "description": "Test only on flows from client hosts never seen in training.\nThis is the axis session-disjointness leaves uncontrolled on a backbone corpus. Grouping by capture day does not separate clients: 33% of the 48,072 distinct client addresses in CESNET-QUIC22 appear on more than one day.\nCaveat that must travel with the number: the median client contributes one flow and only 241 contribute a hundred or more, so the partition is dominated by a small number of heavy clients. It is a real control, not a clean one.\n",
